IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) -- baseline-2026-11: the dates and the s 3A classes that the other modules share.
-- The only module that imports daydate. BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Shared: commencement days and the s 3A classes`

§§ `Commencement days (from the compilation table of the deposited text)`

-- Civil Liability Legislation Amendment (Child Sexual Abuse Actions) Act 2018 (No. 3 of 2018) Part 2, which inserted Part 2A
-- (s 5 of that Act): "1 Jul 2018 (see s. 2(b) and Gazette 29 Jun 2018 p. 2434)". ss 15C(7), 15E(5), 15L(3)(b), (4) count
-- from that day.
`the day Part 2A commenced` MEANS Date 1 7 2018

-- s 15AO(1): "proclamation day means the day on which the Civil Liability Amendment (Provisional Damages for Dust Diseases)
-- Act 2024 Part 2 comes into operation". Compilation table: "1 Dec 2024 (see s. 2(d) and SL 2024/238 cl. 2)".
`proclamation day` MEANS Date 1 12 2024

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is before Part 2A commenced` d IF d BELOW `the day Part 2A commenced`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is before proclamation day` d IF d BELOW `proclamation day`

§§ `s 3A -- the classes of damages the Act's Parts do not reach`

-- s 3A(1): "The provisions of this Act specified in the third column of an item in the Table ... do not apply to damages of a
-- class specified in the second column". The third column, as it touches Part 2 Divisions 3 to 5:
--   item 1 (intentional harm, sexual offence or unlawful sexual conduct): "Parts 1A, 1C, 1CA, 1D, 1E and 2 (other than
--          section 10A)" -- Divisions 3, 4 and 5 all off;
--   item 2 (Motor Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943 damages): "Parts 1C, 1E and 2 (other than section 10A and
--          Division 4)" -- Division 4 kept; Divisions 3 and 5 off;
--   item 3 (Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023 Part 7 Division 2): "... 2 (other than section 10A and
--          Divisions 4 and 5)" -- Divisions 4 and 5 kept; Division 3 off;
--   item 4 (tobacco): "... 2 (other than section 10A and Division 4)" -- Division 4 kept; Divisions 3 and 5 off;
--   item 5 (Civil Aviation (Carriers' Liability) Act 1961): "... and 2" -- all of Part 2 off;
--   item 6 (inhaling asbestos or silica): "... 2 (other than section 10A and Divisions 4 and 5)" -- Divisions 4 and 5 kept;
--          Division 3 off.
-- Part 2A is in no item's third column, so it reaches every class. Each item also takes away Part 2 Division 1, and with it
-- s 6(4) (Part 2 only for incidents after it commenced): for those classes the kept Divisions have no start-date limit.
-- Whether another Act applies to the damages is a borrowed question, asked as a fact.
DECLARE `The class of my damages under s 3A` IS ONE OF
    `none of the s 3A classes`
    `item 1: an unlawful act intended to cause personal injury, a sexual offence or other unlawful sexual conduct`
    `item 2: damages the Motor Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943 applies to`
    `item 3: a claim against my employer under Part 7 Division 2 of the Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023`
    `item 4: smoking or other use of tobacco products`
    `item 5: damages under the Civil Aviation (Carriers' Liability) Act 1961`
    `item 6: inhaling asbestos or silica, and no other item`

-- Part 2 Division 3 (ss 11-13A) is off for every item.
GIVEN c IS A `The class of my damages under s 3A`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Division 3 is taken away by s 3A` IF
    NOT (c EQUALS `none of the s 3A classes`)

-- Part 2 Division 4 (ss 14-15) is off for items 1 and 5 only.
GIVEN c IS A `The class of my damages under s 3A`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Division 4 is taken away by s 3A` IF
       c EQUALS `item 1: an unlawful act intended to cause personal injury, a sexual offence or other unlawful sexual conduct`
    OR c EQUALS `item 5: damages under the Civil Aviation (Carriers' Liability) Act 1961`

-- Part 2 Division 5 (ss 15AA-15AO) is kept for items 3 and 6 only. A dust disease always falls in item 6 (s 15AB: it results
-- from "the inhalation of asbestos or silica"); this function is asked of a dust disease, so `none of the s 3A classes` is
-- read as item 6 alone. A claim that also falls in item 1, 2, 4 or 5 loses Division 5 under that item.
GIVEN c IS A `The class of my damages under s 3A`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Division 5 is taken away by s 3A` IF
       c EQUALS `item 1: an unlawful act intended to cause personal injury, a sexual offence or other unlawful sexual conduct`
    OR c EQUALS `item 2: damages the Motor Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943 applies to`
    OR c EQUALS `item 4: smoking or other use of tobacco products`
    OR c EQUALS `item 5: damages under the Civil Aviation (Carriers' Liability) Act 1961`

-- s 6(1), (4), (5): Part 2 applies "only if the personal injury arises out of an incident happening after the commencement of
-- this Part"; if that "cannot be ascertained", the incident is taken to be after if "the symptoms of the injury first
-- appeared after" it. The date (1 January 2003, the encoder's reading in baseline-2026-10) is the person's fact. s 6 is
-- itself in Part 2 Division 1, so it binds only claims in none of the s 3A classes.
GIVEN c IS A `The class of my damages under s 3A`, `after Part 2 commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6(4) keeps Part 2 out` IF
        c EQUALS `none of the s 3A classes`
    AND (NOT `after Part 2 commenced`)
